! TWX Script Commands

!! GETCOURSES

`GETCOURSES` returns every unique shortest directed course between two sectors.

Syntax:

{{{
getcourses $courses $source $destination
}}}

Arguments:

* `$courses`: output array to populate.
* `$source`: starting sector.
* `$destination`: ending sector.

Return structure:

* `$courses` scalar value is the number of shortest courses returned.
* `$courses[n]` is one complete course.
* `$courses[n]` scalar value is the course hop count, matching `GETCOURSE`.
* `$courses[n][1]` through `$courses[n][m]` contain the sector numbers from source through destination, matching the path-array structure returned by `GETCOURSE`.

Ordering:

* `$courses[1]` is seeded from the legacy TWX/Pascal breadth-first path.
* `$courses[2]` is seeded from the current `GETCOURSE` bidirectional path when that route is different.
* Remaining equal-hop routes are then enumerated in stored warp order.
* If legacy BFS and current `GETCOURSE` pick the same route, it is returned only once because `GETCOURSES` returns unique courses.

Example:

{{{
getcourses $courses 14952 7635
echo "courses=" $courses "*"
echo "first hop count=" $courses[1] "*"
echo "first sector=" $courses[1][1] "*"
}}}

Notes:

* Only shortest courses are returned. Longer alternate routes are not included.
* Avoided sectors are honored using the same active avoid list as pathing commands.
* The command was appended to the end of the TWX30 native command table to avoid shifting existing compiled command IDs.
